---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="Install the a11ied agent skill"
   summary="The skill teaches coding agents how to choose a11ied commands, combine axe with screen reader testing, and report what the evidence actually proves."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Recommended install</p>
            <h2>Install it with aix</h2>
         </div>
         <p><a href="http://aix.a1st.dev/">aix</a> finds the coding agents on your machine and asks which one should receive the skill. User scope makes it available to that agent in every project.</p>
         <pre><code>npx -y @a1st/aix install https://github.com/hypothesi/a11ied/blob/master/packages/skills/ai.json --only skills --user</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">One agent only</div>
         <p class="aside-note">Add <code>--target codex</code>, <code>--target claude-code</code>, or another supported target to skip the editor prompt.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Getting started</p>
         <h2>Give the agent a page and a job</h2>
      </div>
      <ol>
         <li>Install the <code>a1</code> command if it is not already available.</li>
         <li>Restart your coding agent so it discovers the new skill.</li>
         <li>Start the website or app you want to test.</li>
         <li>Tell the agent which route and behavior to check.</li>
      </ol>
      <pre><code>npm install --global a11ied

a1 doctor</code></pre>
      <pre data-label="AI AGENT PROMPT"><code>Use the a11ied skill to test http://localhost:3000/checkout.
Run the automated checks first, then test the form labels and error messages
with the available screen reader. Keep the findings and transcript separate.</code></pre>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">What the skill changes</p>
         <h2>A repeatable testing workflow</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Chooses the right interface</strong><span>Uses repeatable CLI commands by default and MCP when the agent has a11ied tools connected.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Checks coverage first</strong><span>Looks up the WCAG criterion and its automation coverage before choosing axe or a screen reader.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Uses real assistive technology when needed</strong><span>Starts with the virtual reader for quick feedback, then moves to VoiceOver or NVDA when their behavior matters.</span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Keeps claims honest</strong><span>Separates automated results, transcripts, and human judgment instead of calling every passing scan compliant.</span></div>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Use with MCP</p>
            <h2>Let the agent call a11ied directly</h2>
         </div>
         <p>The skill tells the agent how to work. The MCP server gives it tools for WCAG lookup, axe scans, and screen reader sessions.</p>
         <p>Follow the <a href="/agent-workflows">AI agent guide</a> to connect MCP and run a practical test. Use the <a href="/mcp-usage">MCP tool reference</a> when you need exact inputs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">Skill source</div>
         <p class="aside-note">The installed instructions come from <code>packages/skills/a11ied/SKILL.md</code> in this repository.</p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Update the skill</p>
         <h2>Run the install command again</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Run the same <code>aix install</code> command again to pull the current skill from the repository and reinstall it at user scope.</p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
